' lint-ok: a building block is no business process, so it owns no BPxx call sites (ADR-069)
@startbpmn BB05_EditState
lang en

output L1 "BB05_EditState.bpmn"

' One gesture that carries its own value: a flag, a position, a placement. A member words the
' gesture in its own verb - pause or resume, order, rank, drag - and the placeholders hold the slot.
' Nothing is composed, so nothing drafts - and the write is attempted rather than assumed: the
' answer carries the outcome, which is what lets a client compare what happened against what it
' predicted and catch a defect instead of drifting out of sync. The chain is EditContent's chain
' with another verb in the box.

pool "User" {
  :Set the <entity>'s <state>;
  send "Set a <entity>'s <state>" to stateIn
  receive "The <state> outcome" as outcome
  end "Back on the surface"
}

system pool "Bearing" {
  messageStart "<State> submitted" as stateIn
  ' lint-ok: BB05.01 names the block's canonical chain; a call site is minted by a process's own drawing
  call "BB05.01_SetTheState" "Set a <entity>'s <state>" {
    if "Does a rule refuse the change?" rule BR-128 then "yes"
      :Refuse the change and say why;
    else "no"
      :Apply the change;
    endif
    :Report the outcome;
  }
  send "The <state> outcome" to outcome
  note "A state is its own act where it has an owner or a consequence beyond the record; otherwise it is a field of the editor. Where the answer also raises a further act - a move that put an activity's last task into Done - that is the member's own business."
  end "<State> answered"
}

@endbpmn
